    "lawCode": "Amd Part CC §8, Chap 57 of 2014",
    "lawSection": "Rockland County",
    "memo": "BILL NUMBER:S4858\n\nTITLE OF BILL:  An act to amend section 8 of part CC of chapter 57 of\nthe laws of 2014 relating to the \"Rockland Bergen Flood Mitigation\nact\" and creating the Rockland Bergen Flood Mitigation Task Force, in\nrelation to the effectiveness thereof\n\nPURPOSE: This bill will extend the effectiveness of the Rockland\nBergen Flood Mitigation Act to two years following the organization of\nthe task force\n\nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1 amends section 8 of part CC of chapter 57 of the laws of\n2014 relating to the \"Rockland Bergen Flood Mitigation Act\" and\ncreating the Rockland Bergen Flood Mitigation Task Force, which shall\nexpire two years following the date of the organization of the task\nforce.\n\nJUSTIFICATION:  This bill will extend the expiration date of the\n\"Rockland Bergen Flood Mitigation Act\" to two years following the\norganization of the task force. The task force is set to expire on\nJune 30, 2016 but has not yet organized Appointments are being made to\nthe task force but they have yet to meet. This law would ensure that\nthe task force is given an appropriate amount of time to study the\ncomplex issues of flooding before the act is repealed.\n\nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY: New bill.\n\nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS: None\n\nEFFECTIVE DATE:  This act shall take effect on the same date and in\nthe same manner as section 8 of part cc of chapter 57 of the laws of\n2014 relating to the \"Rockland Bergen Flood Mitigation act\" and\ncreating the Rockland Bergen Flood Mitigation Task Force takes effect.\n\n",
